FLOW1
# f02: the CPU path -> m01 params (falcon / CPU marth d1 / ystory).
#
# RE-AUTHORED for the CSS mechanics arc (docs/MENU-SPEC.md items 1+2+3+4).
# The leg exercises every gesture this screen has: token grab with B,
# carry-and-hover across the whole roster, drop with A, the clickable port
# type box run twice (N/A -> HMN -> CPU, css.js:348-357), and the CPU
# level as a GRAB-DRAG KNOB rather than a stepper (css.js:316-334 /
# 396-408, DEVIATION D7). The knob drag ends by pushing PAST the rail's
# low end, so the x clamp (css.js:318-320) is still the witness it was:
# the frozen trace shows difficulty settling at 1 and no further event.
#
# CLAMP-ANCHORED POSITIONING — see the note in f01-vs-g01.flow. Every
# cursor stop below is reached by holding into a screen edge and then
# counting frames away from it, so a +/-1 device-frame timing error on
# the wall-clock injector cannot move which widget the hand is over.
I 1 -
I 375 S
I 376 -
I 380 A
I 381 -
# Anchor UP x70 (y clamps to 0), then DOWN x12 -> y = 46.08: the roster
# band (26,62) and the cell row (32,62), x still 28.00 = cell 0.
I 390 U
I 460 -
I 465 D
I 477 -
# B retrieves P1's token to the hand (css.js:209-215).
I 480 B
I 483 -
# Carry RIGHT x77 -> x = 212.80, inside cell 4 (190,234) = falcon. The
# hover-select fires once per cell crossed (css.js:222-226).
I 490 R
I 567 -
# A drops the token on falcon and plays its announcer (css.js:293).
I 575 A
I 578 -
# To port 2's type tab: anchor LEFT+DOWN x105, then RIGHT x33 ->
# x = 79.20 and UP x36 -> y = 101.76.
I 585 LD
I 690 -
I 695 R
I 728 -
I 733 U
I 769 -
# A twice: N/A -> HMN -> CPU (togglePort, main.js:504-520 with DEVIATION
# D5's NET dropped). The CPU panel and its level knob only exist while
# the port is CPU (css.js:937-969), so this is what makes the knob below
# reachable at all.
I 775 A
I 778 -
I 785 A
I 788 -
# To the knob: anchor LEFT+DOWN x105 again, then RIGHT x40 -> x = 96.00
# (the knob's default-level centre, +/-6 hit box) and UP x13 ->
# y = 190.08 (the rail sits at y = 189.00).
I 795 LD
I 900 -
I 905 R
I 945 -
I 950 U
I 963 -
# A grabs the knob (css.js:396-408). The hand is now LOCKED to the rail.
I 970 A
I 973 -
# Drag LEFT x15. The level is re-derived from the hand position every
# frame (css.js:325-327): 3 -> 2 -> 1, and the last frames run into the
# rail's low clamp at x = 72.00, which produces no further event.
I 980 L
I 995 -
# NOTE the drag deliberately ENDS on the clamp (x = 72.00), which is also
# level 1's stop, so this flow's frozen shot cannot by itself witness that the
# slider is CONTINUOUS. It cannot: level 1's band is [72,78), only 6.00 px
# wide, while the translator's 3-frame minimum for a direction press moves the
# hand 7.20 px — no authored press can land inside that band off its stop. The
# slider's continuity is NOT witnessed by any host check (see the note on T6
# in check-foh-flows.sh — the structural trace cannot see a render position,
# and the shot arm only compares run A to run B). The clamp witness stays
# here, where upstream's arm is (css.js:318-320).
# A releases the knob (css.js:328-333); allowRegrab stops the same frame
# from re-grabbing it.
I 1005 A
I 1008 -
SHOT 1015 css-cpu
I 1020 S
I 1023 -
I 1030 R
I 1033 -
SHOT 1040 sss-ystory
I 1045 A
I 1048 -
END 1055
